# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Fine-tuning on one A100 (about 20 s per epoch) or four A100s (56-78 min per epoch); INS spectra from the MLIPs take minutes on a personal computer versus days of DFT (main text).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The SI reports 'fitting' RMSEs without naming the evaluation split; they are recorded as training errors. Stress RMSEs are in meV/A3 (unit null).
# - INS spectra, peak assignments (Table 2), lattice parameters (Table 1) and MD validations (Table 3) are properties. The base checkpoints are named as in the SI; their sizes are not stated.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/armstrong2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

